<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cayor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cayor was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> kingdom in what is now western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>, one of the constituent states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a>. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic trade</a> expanded in the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries, Cayor gained direct access to European goods and revenues. It broke away from Jolof in the sixteenth century, contributing to the empire's fragmentation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cayor.jpg" alt="Cayor" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cheikh Khadim Rassoul D. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_Of_Cayor2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
